# SOLVENT_DATABASE_URL is the LIVE indexer database (the backfill daemon's).
SOLVENT_DATABASE_URL=postgres://solvent:solvent@localhost:5432/solvent?sslmode=disable
SOLVENT_RPC_OP=https://mainnet.optimism.io
SOLVENT_RPC_ETH=https://eth.llamarpc.com
SOLVENT_POLL_INTERVAL=5s
# Collateral snapshot sweep cadence (default 1h) and price poll cadence
# (default 1m); Go duration strings, must be positive.
#SOLVENT_SNAPSHOT_INTERVAL=1h
#SOLVENT_PRICE_INTERVAL=1m
# Health/readiness endpoint bind address (default 127.0.0.1:9090; "off"
# disables the listener).
#SOLVENT_HEALTH_ADDR=127.0.0.1:9090
# TEST_DATABASE_URL points at the SCRATCH database solvent_test — NEVER at
# `solvent`: the store test suite Migrate+TRUNCATEs twelve tables including
# raw_logs, so aiming it at the live database destroys the backfill (Task 9
# wave 10 DB split; `make db-up` provisions solvent_test idempotently, and
# cmd/reconcile refuses to run when both DSNs resolve to one database).
# NOTE: this variable must actually be PRESENT in your local .env, not merely
# here — every live-db test in the repo silently SKIPS in dev mode when it is
# unset, so a suite that looks green may have run almost nothing. Verify with
# `go test ./internal/store/ -run TestWriteRiskBatchRoundTrip -v` (it should
# PASS, not SKIP). `make test-acceptance` makes the omission fatal.
TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://solvent:solvent@localhost:5432/solvent_test?sslmode=disable
# cmd/reconcile RPC overrides (fall back to SOLVENT_RPC_* when unset). The
# ETH recon endpoint must be ARCHIVE-STATE capable: the W1 golden row is a
# live pinned eth_call at block 25,584,990, which non-archive endpoints
# reject as pruned. Keys belong in your local .env only — never committed.
#SOLVENT_RECON_RPC_ETH=
#SOLVENT_RECON_RPC_OP=
# Read-only evidence tests (invariants_live_test.go) gate on this — point it
# at the live database for the receipt run; the connection is forced
# read-only and never migrates.
#SOLVENT_RECON_DATABASE_URL=
# --- cmd/riskd (P3 Task 5, the risk materializer) --------------------------
# SOLVENT_RISKD_DATABASE_URL is riskd's OWN database URL, and the reason it is
# separate from SOLVENT_DATABASE_URL is structural: migration 00013 creates a
# `solvent_riskd` role with SELECT-only on the P2 tables and full DML on the
# risk tables, so "riskd never writes indexer state" is enforced by the
# database rather than by review (design spec §2, chain-truth R6.6).
#
# The role is created NOLOGIN and carries NO password — a credential committed
# to a migration is a credential published to everyone who clones the repo. To
# use it, grant login yourself:
#
#   ALTER ROLE solvent_riskd LOGIN PASSWORD '<pick-one>';
#   SOLVENT_RISKD_DATABASE_URL=postgres://solvent_riskd:<pick-one>@localhost:5432/solvent?sslmode=disable
#
# Unset falls back to SOLVENT_DATABASE_URL so a local run works immediately;
# riskd logs a WARNING in that case, because the read-only posture is then not
# in force. riskd never migrates — the indexer owns the schema.
#SOLVENT_RISKD_DATABASE_URL=
# Watermark-vector poll cadence (default 2s). riskd recomputes only when the
# vector actually moves, compared by (last_block, acked_epoch) per engine.
#SOLVENT_RISK_POLL_INTERVAL=2s
# Risk-batch retention: keep the newest N batches, pruned inside each write
# transaction (default 5000).
#SOLVENT_RISK_RETENTION=5000
# Price freshness budget for VALUATION inputs (default 3m = 3x the 60s poll
# cadence). Past this an input is stale-and-flagged (G4); past TWICE this it is
# refused as a missing input (G1, the design's R = 2 x T_f). Every input riskd
# values with is a POLL row, and a poll oracle has no publication heartbeat to
# be stale against — so this is repo POLICY derived from our own cadence, NOT a
# published feed heartbeat. That is why the B3 unverified-heartbeat escalation
# does not gate riskd (it still gates cmd/api's stream-row verdicts).
#SOLVENT_RISK_PRICE_BUDGET=3m
# Single-interval price-move bound in basis points (default 2000 = 20%). A move
# beyond it is FLAGGED and disclosed as policy, never refused: the polled price
# IS the engine's charging price. 0 disables the flag.
#SOLVENT_RISK_STEP_BPS=2000
# Path to Foundry's anvil binary (not on PATH) — opts in the fork-replay test (internal/forkreplay); unset = skip.
#ANVIL_BIN=
# Archive-capable OP RPC URL anvil forks from (the dRPC OP endpoint works) — unset = the fork-replay test skips.
#ANVIL_FORK_RPC=
# Archive-capable ETH MAINNET RPC URL anvil forks from — opts in the P3 Task 3
# pipeline-replay harness (internal/pipelinereplay, `make test-pipeline-replay`)
# together with ANVIL_BIN; unset = its legs skip. Deliberately SEPARATE from
# ANVIL_FORK_RPC above, which is the OP endpoint Task 10 forks.
#
# It must be ARCHIVE-COMPLETE: the legs fork ETH mainnet at blocks 20,714,020
# and 21,469,984, and anvil PROXIES every pre-fork eth_getLogs/eth_call to this
# upstream. A free-tier Alchemy key is the sanctioned choice here (probe A3's
# targeted carve-out: opt-in, on-demand, ~100 getLogs per full run) — the
# harness therefore walks at WINDOW 10, because the upstream's 10-block getLogs
# cap becomes the harness's cap. Never point bulk backfill traffic at this key.
#ANVIL_FORK_RPC_ETH=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# cmd/api — the public REST + SSE read surface (P3 Task 7)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The api's database URL. Preferred over SOLVENT_DATABASE_URL for the same
# reason riskd's is: this service only ever SELECTs, so it belongs on a
# credential that structurally cannot write. Migration 00013 provisions the
# SELECT-only `solvent_riskd` role NOLOGIN with no password; grant it LOGIN with
# a password of your choosing and point this at it:
#
#   ALTER ROLE solvent_riskd LOGIN PASSWORD '<pick-one>';
#   SOLVENT_API_DATABASE_URL=postgres://solvent_riskd:<pick-one>@localhost:5432/solvent?sslmode=disable
#
# Unset falls back to SOLVENT_DATABASE_URL so a local run works immediately; api
# logs a WARNING in that case, because the read-only posture is then not in
# force. api NEVER migrates and REFUSES to start against a database whose goose
# version is not the one this build's queries were written against.
#SOLVENT_API_DATABASE_URL=
# Listen address (default :8080).
#SOLVENT_API_ADDR=:8080
# Per-CLIENT-ADDRESS token bucket: sustained requests per second and burst
# (defaults 20 / 40). The key is the CONNECTION's remote address, never an
# X-Forwarded-For header — a client-supplied header is a client-chosen bucket,
# which is not a rate limit. Deploying behind a proxy needs a deliberate
# decision about which header to trust; that is P5 deployment work.
#SOLVENT_API_RATE_LIMIT=20
#SOLVENT_API_RATE_BURST=40
# How long an idle per-address bucket survives before eviction (default 10m).
# It bounds the limiter map against a source-address scan.
#SOLVENT_API_RATE_TTL=10m
# SSE cadences. The heartbeat is a COMMENT frame, so an idle stream stays
# distinguishable from a dead one through a buffering proxy (default 15s). The
# poll is the NOTIFY fallback: PostgreSQL drops queued notifications on
# reconnect, so the poll is the mechanism and the doorbell is the optimization
# (default 5s).
#SOLVENT_API_SSE_HEARTBEAT=15s
#SOLVENT_API_SSE_POLL=5s
# Default number of batches /v1/observatory returns (default 50, max 500).
#SOLVENT_API_OBSERVATORY_LIMIT=50
# The committed scenario whose SINGLE axis the /v1/book waterfall grid walks
# (default eth_minus_60 — ETH is the factor essentially the whole book is
# exposed to, so its monotonicity invariant is the meaningful one).
#
# THE TAIL-RUNG INVARIANT: this line and the grid line below are NOT independent
# knobs. The frontier publishes no disclosures of its own — it borrows THIS
# scenario's out_of_model and path_assumption wholesale — so the grid's LAST
# point must equal THIS scenario's own committed shock, exactly. eth_minus_60
# commits 40/100, so the tail must be 400000000000000000 and nothing else.
# Startup REFUSES a mismatched pair (naming both values) rather than serving a
# deepest point whose small print describes a different shock. Change one line
# here and you must change the other; going deeper means COMMITTING the matching
# scenario rung first.
#SOLVENT_API_WATERFALL_SCENARIO=eth_minus_60
# The waterfall grid: comma-separated WAD-scaled factors, STRICTLY DESCENDING.
# The default opens at 1e18 — the UNSHOCKED book — because that point is where
# the standing bad-debt census comes from; relabelling a shocked point as
# "current" would be a fabrication. It closes at 4e17, the committed shock of
# the scenario named above (see the tail-rung invariant).
#SOLVENT_API_WATERFALL_GRID=1000000000000000000,900000000000000000,800000000000000000,700000000000000000,600000000000000000,500000000000000000,400000000000000000
